1
00:00:06,132 --> 00:00:08,050
<i>All I did was love a guy.</i>

2
00:00:08,134 --> 00:00:09,885
You loved a married man.

3
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:11,971
<i>Come home, Beth, please?</i>

4
00:00:12,054 --> 00:00:13,931
We will all be waiting for you here.

5
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,766
<i>He's a good man.</i>

6
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:17,810
<i>- He's good...</i>
- <i>He's good at lying!</i>

7
00:00:17,893 --> 00:00:20,855
<i>Have I told you</i>
<i>it's not just Joel he'd killed?</i>

8
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:22,732
He killed Papa too.

9
00:00:22,815 --> 00:00:24,316
You believe her?

10
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,485
<i>Well, life is like that.</i>
<i>We're all just using each other.</i>

11
00:00:26,569 --> 00:00:28,946
Even though De Castro killed my dad,

12
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:31,699
you're the reason why there's still
no justice for his death!

13
00:00:31,782 --> 00:00:34,201
<i>You should be the one</i>
<i>tied and locked up.</i>

14
00:00:35,619 --> 00:00:37,621
<i>Regina isn't the crazy one here.</i>

15
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:41,208
- It's you.
- Fuck you, Mara.

16
00:00:41,292 --> 00:00:42,668
- Stay away from me!
- Please, listen to me!

17
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:45,296
Mara!

18
00:00:46,422 --> 00:00:47,965
<i>This can't be happening!</i>

19
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:50,551
<i>Ben, this is all my fault!</i>

20
00:00:51,927 --> 00:00:55,264
This is all my fault... Mara...

21
00:00:56,766 --> 00:00:58,350
What are you thinking of?

22
00:00:59,101 --> 00:01:00,144
Us.

23
00:01:00,895 --> 00:01:03,063
- Huh? Us?
- Mm.

24
00:01:04,523 --> 00:01:06,525
<i>If we're going to have a child.</i>

25
00:01:13,282 --> 00:01:14,450
Do you want one?

26
00:01:16,327 --> 00:01:17,870
Do we want one?

27
00:01:18,746 --> 00:01:19,872
I do.

28
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:23,918
How about you?

29
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:31,759
What if it's not meant to be?

30
00:01:34,512 --> 00:01:36,931
I'm just scared that...

31
00:01:37,014 --> 00:01:39,642
we won't have a peaceful life.

32
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:43,854
That's not the kind of life
I want for our child.

33
00:01:44,688 --> 00:01:47,274
You know how my life was before, Ben.

34
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:52,988
We will be different.

35
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:55,991
I promise.

36
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:02,832
We will be better as parents.

37
00:02:38,784 --> 00:02:40,536
This way, ma'am.

38
00:02:40,619 --> 00:02:42,538
Ma'am, you're bleeding.
We need a wheelchair!

39
00:02:42,621 --> 00:02:45,249
No, no.
No, I-- I need Dr. Bueno.

40
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:47,418
Doc, emergency!

41
00:02:47,501 --> 00:02:49,086
Female with active bleeding!

42
00:02:49,503 --> 00:02:51,088
Careful, ma'am.

43
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:02,224
Dr. Bueno, please.

44
00:03:02,725 --> 00:03:03,767
Doc!

45
00:03:09,273 --> 00:03:12,318
Ben, that was Mara...

46
00:03:12,401 --> 00:03:14,111
Let me talk to my sister.

47
00:03:14,194 --> 00:03:16,947
Mara... It's my fault, Ben.

48
00:03:17,031 --> 00:03:18,407
No, Ging.

49
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:19,742
Ben, is it my fault?

50
00:03:19,825 --> 00:03:22,036
- It's not your fault.
- Mara...

51
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:23,829
- It's not your fault.
- That was Mara.

52
00:03:23,913 --> 00:03:25,331
It wasn't Mara.

53
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:28,751
I'll fix this, okay?

54
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:30,294
- I'll fix this.
- It was Mara.

55
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:33,464
No. It was a stranger.

56
00:03:34,423 --> 00:03:37,343
- It was a stranger.
- No, I saw it...

57
00:03:37,426 --> 00:03:39,261
I saw it. It was me!

58
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:41,889
Stay in the car.

59
00:03:41,972 --> 00:03:43,557
- I'll be back.
- I don't want to.

60
00:03:43,641 --> 00:03:45,768
- I don't want to.
- I'll just talk to the police.

61
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:47,519
I'll explain to them
that it wasn't your fault.

62
00:03:47,603 --> 00:03:48,938
- I don't want to.
- It's okay, Ging.

63
00:03:49,021 --> 00:03:50,856
I'll explain to them it wasn't your fault.

64
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:52,232
I don't want to.

65
00:03:52,316 --> 00:03:54,568
- I'll be right back.
- Okay, sir.

66
00:03:54,652 --> 00:03:57,154
- I don't want to, Ben!
- I'll come and get you.

67
00:04:04,119 --> 00:04:07,790
Attorney. Do you know the woman?

68
00:04:08,916 --> 00:04:10,334
I don't know her.

69
00:04:12,336 --> 00:04:13,963
Does your sister know her?

70
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:18,384
I doubt it. My sister has
a mental health problem.

71
00:04:20,678 --> 00:04:24,098
Chief, if you have other questions,
just direct them to me.

72
00:04:24,890 --> 00:04:27,393
- Okay, Attorney. Thank you.
- Okay. Thank you.

73
00:04:35,943 --> 00:04:37,695
Mrs. Santos?

74
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:41,156
Mrs. Santos?

75
00:04:46,370 --> 00:04:47,621
Ana?

76
00:04:49,123 --> 00:04:51,041
There's nothing to worry.

77
00:04:51,125 --> 00:04:55,546
The ultrasound showed
that you have a subchorionic hematoma.

78
00:04:55,629 --> 00:04:58,298
You experienced bleeding

79
00:04:58,382 --> 00:05:01,135
because a blood vessel ruptured

80
00:05:01,218 --> 00:05:05,389
between your uterine lining
and the baby's gestational sac.

81
00:05:10,352 --> 00:05:11,854
I'm pregnant?

82
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:14,231
Yes. Six weeks.

83
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:21,363
Bleeding during pregnancy
can be frightening, but don't worry.

84
00:05:21,447 --> 00:05:22,948
We will monitor.

85
00:05:23,907 --> 00:05:27,828
But I want to tell you now
that the baby is safe.

86
00:05:31,123 --> 00:05:33,125
Would you like me to call Attorney?

87
00:05:33,709 --> 00:05:34,877
No.

88
00:05:36,336 --> 00:05:39,757
Let me be the one to...
to tell him the good news.

89
00:05:40,674 --> 00:05:42,009
All right, all right.

90
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:44,928
- I'll fix your release papers.
- Okay.

91
00:06:30,474 --> 00:06:32,226
So, are you ready, bro?

92
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:34,394
Yeah, I'm almost ready.

93
00:06:34,478 --> 00:06:38,899
If we find any treasure,
we'll split it evenly, all right?

94
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:40,984
You won't find any treasure in Vallente.

95
00:06:41,068 --> 00:06:42,653
You're more likely to find a mermaid.

96
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:44,571
You're crazy, bro.

97
00:06:44,655 --> 00:06:47,241
- Let's start the engine.
- Let's go.

98
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:00,898

Please pick up.

99
00:08:01,398 --> 00:08:02,900


100
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:13,327
Ana? Hello.

101
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:14,828
Ana.

102
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:18,081
They're looking for you
at the church. Where are you?

103
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:20,167
Are you going to the reception?

104
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:21,835
No.

105
00:08:23,086 --> 00:08:25,088
Something happened.

106
00:08:26,465 --> 00:08:29,134
<i>What? What happened?</i>

107
00:08:31,553 --> 00:08:34,389
I'm heading home.
We can talk then.

108
00:08:34,473 --> 00:08:35,974
No, Ana.

109
00:08:36,558 --> 00:08:37,809
Ana, tell me what happened.

110
00:08:38,352 --> 00:08:40,020
Let's talk at home, Ben.

111
00:08:40,646 --> 00:08:42,314
<i>Okay. I'm heading home. Wait for me.</i>

112
00:08:43,065 --> 00:08:45,317
I'll see you.
Take care.

113
00:08:50,447 --> 00:08:51,782


114
00:08:59,748 --> 00:09:02,793


115
00:09:44,668 --> 00:09:46,086
- Sir.
Sir.

116
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:47,337
Good morning, sir.

117
00:09:47,421 --> 00:09:49,006
- Jose.
Sir.

118
00:09:49,089 --> 00:09:51,842
- What did they find out at sea?
Over here, sir.

119
00:10:08,692 --> 00:10:10,944
Looks like
it was dumped a long time ago.

120
00:10:11,028 --> 00:10:12,279
I agree, sir.

121
00:10:12,738 --> 00:10:13,780
Okay.

122
00:10:16,241 --> 00:10:18,660


123
00:10:22,956 --> 00:10:25,876


124
00:10:26,335 --> 00:10:27,919
I spoke to her earlier.

125
00:10:28,003 --> 00:10:30,714
She said she was heading home,
but she's still not here.

126
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:33,633
And I called Katrina.
She said that Ana didn't call her.

127
00:10:34,343 --> 00:10:36,011
<i>Did something happen again?</i>

128
00:10:37,721 --> 00:10:40,807
<i>Ana wouldn't go missing</i>
<i>if nothing happened.</i>

129
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:45,729
I'll ask for help with looking for her.

130
00:10:45,812 --> 00:10:49,649
Ben, it should be you who finds Ana.

131
00:10:50,067 --> 00:10:51,818
Resolve it as soon as possible.

132
00:11:03,997 --> 00:11:05,248
Okay.

133
00:11:06,458 --> 00:11:07,751
Okay, Ana.

134
00:11:10,087 --> 00:11:12,089
Shit, that's really far.

135
00:11:20,764 --> 00:11:22,557
What are you doing out there?

136
00:11:25,769 --> 00:11:27,521
Why are you out there?

137
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:30,774


138
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:32,150


139
00:11:34,027 --> 00:11:36,863
Calm down. She's not missing.

140
00:11:36,947 --> 00:11:39,991
We can't contact Beth.
We don't know where she is.

141
00:11:40,075 --> 00:11:41,368
We already checked.

142
00:11:41,451 --> 00:11:43,954
Her flight was not canceled.

143
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:47,207
Maybe she didn't leave.
Maybe she's still in Vallente.

144
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:50,293
She would've told us
if she wasn't leaving.

145
00:11:51,795 --> 00:11:55,215
Maybe she's already here,
but she made a quick stop first.

146
00:11:55,298 --> 00:11:57,134
Or maybe her phone died.

147
00:11:57,217 --> 00:12:00,637
There are other explanations
aside from her going missing.

148
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:06,601
Why don't we ask Attorney Ben?

149
00:12:06,685 --> 00:12:08,061
- Maybe--
No!

150
00:12:10,564 --> 00:12:12,816
I mean, let me handle that.

151
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,902
I'll ask the people I know in Vallente.

152
00:12:15,986 --> 00:12:18,155
If I don't hear anything,
we'll check with the airline

153
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:19,990
if she got on her flight.

154
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:23,368
That's all we can do for now.

155
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:51,141
Shit, Ana. Where are you?

156
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:00,817
Thank you, Nanny.

157
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:04,571
What's that?

158
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:09,326
I just picked up some of Papa's stuff.

159
00:15:12,579 --> 00:15:15,165
Why'd you come at such a late hour?

160
00:15:17,334 --> 00:15:20,462
Actually, ma'am,
I wanted to say goodbye to you.

161
00:15:21,588 --> 00:15:23,173
Now that Papa's gone,

162
00:15:23,882 --> 00:15:26,635
I have no reason to stay in Vallente.

163
00:15:31,514 --> 00:15:33,850
So, you're here to ask for money?

164
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,185
Ah, no.

165
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:38,188
I just wanted to say goodbye.

166
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,235
Ma'am Imelda,

167
00:15:44,819 --> 00:15:46,738
thank you so much for everything.

168
00:15:49,574 --> 00:15:54,079
I am forever grateful to you
for giving my father a proper funeral.

169
00:16:01,503 --> 00:16:02,754
Juancho.

170
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:04,964
Ma'am?

171
00:16:09,803 --> 00:16:12,305
Just in case you need a place to stay...

172
00:16:14,099 --> 00:16:16,101
you can come back anytime.

173
00:16:47,048 --> 00:16:50,552
<i>Babes, I'm here</i>
<i>at my contact's meeting place.</i>

174
00:17:19,497 --> 00:17:21,332
Well, well, well.

175
00:17:22,167 --> 00:17:23,501
Bridgette.

176
00:17:24,419 --> 00:17:25,587
Sir Ramon.

177
00:17:27,130 --> 00:17:28,381
You know what?

178
00:17:29,466 --> 00:17:31,217
I've changed my mind.

179
00:17:32,302 --> 00:17:34,888
Why don't you bring your friend?

180
00:17:35,472 --> 00:17:37,307
The one...

181
00:17:37,891 --> 00:17:39,517
with big...

182
00:17:41,269 --> 00:17:43,438
you-know-what.

183
00:17:46,399 --> 00:17:48,067
Okay, I'll call her...

184
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:51,863
once I'm sure you'll honor the deal.

185
00:17:51,946 --> 00:17:53,698
Well!

186
00:17:54,199 --> 00:17:56,117
Of course I will.

187
00:17:57,827 --> 00:17:59,829
Well then, let's get going.

188
00:18:19,557 --> 00:18:20,809
General.

189
00:18:24,229 --> 00:18:26,564
I want you to release someone

190
00:18:27,774 --> 00:18:31,027
from the Malaysian operation in your area.

191
00:18:32,153 --> 00:18:33,988
The one headed by Eric Mercado.

192
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:37,700
Angel. She's fair-skinned.

193
00:18:38,535 --> 00:18:41,037
Her name is Angel.

194
00:18:41,996 --> 00:18:43,832
Just give her to me.

195
00:18:44,707 --> 00:18:46,459
No, just that one.

196
00:18:47,001 --> 00:18:48,169
Just Angel.

197
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:51,464
Thanks, man.

198
00:18:56,261 --> 00:18:57,762
What did he say?

199
00:19:02,934 --> 00:19:04,352
That's Angel.

200
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:09,941
Well, then...

201
00:19:12,694 --> 00:19:14,946
go and message your friend.

202
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:25,164
Message your friend.

203
00:19:25,248 --> 00:19:28,084
Y-Yes, I'll call her.

204
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:30,169
You don't have to ask me twice.

205
00:19:30,879 --> 00:19:32,297
I'll just...

206
00:19:32,964 --> 00:19:37,802
call her from the restroom
while I'm freshening up.

207
00:19:39,345 --> 00:19:40,680
Make it quick.

208
00:19:41,723 --> 00:19:43,725
I can barely contain myself.

209
00:19:56,738 --> 00:19:57,989
I'll make a call.

210
00:20:10,251 --> 00:20:11,502
<i>Hello?</i>

211
00:20:13,546 --> 00:20:16,633
I need to know the truth about my husband.

212
00:20:20,386 --> 00:20:21,554
Ana...

213
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:23,598
I already know.

214
00:20:24,807 --> 00:20:27,769
I know the truth.
I know that Ben is not a lawyer.

215
00:20:27,852 --> 00:20:30,855
You can't deny it to me
because I already have proof.

216
00:20:31,648 --> 00:20:33,232
Ben is a good lawyer.

217
00:20:33,316 --> 00:20:36,486
I wouldn't send him to Vallente
if he wasn't great.

218
00:20:36,569 --> 00:20:40,114
Oh, come on. I know he's great.

219
00:20:40,198 --> 00:20:43,868
He's so good
that he's deceived a lot of people.

220
00:20:43,952 --> 00:20:45,620
Deceived?

221
00:20:45,703 --> 00:20:47,622
He helped a lot of people.

222
00:20:47,705 --> 00:20:52,377
He fought for the workers
at the <i>azucarera.</i>

223
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:54,379
They did not lose their jobs.

224
00:20:54,462 --> 00:20:56,839
But he's not a real lawyer!

225
00:20:56,923 --> 00:21:01,636
Why does it matter
what you think is real or not, Ana?

226
00:21:01,719 --> 00:21:03,054
Are you his client?

227
00:21:03,137 --> 00:21:05,723
- I am his wife.
- <i>Exactly!</i>

228
00:21:05,807 --> 00:21:08,935
Then why are you questioning
his credentials?

229
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:11,854
You called because
if he was hiding something from others,

230
00:21:11,938 --> 00:21:13,690
he could also be hiding
something from you.

231
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:14,857
Am I right, Ana?

232
00:21:16,943 --> 00:21:18,027
<i>Tell me, Ana.</i>

233
00:21:18,111 --> 00:21:20,488
<i>Did he ever treat you badly</i>
<i>as your husband?</i>

234
00:21:20,571 --> 00:21:24,450
Throughout your relationship,
did he hurt you?

235
00:21:24,534 --> 00:21:27,203
Did he ever hurt you physically?

236
00:21:29,372 --> 00:21:32,583
If one thing about your husband
turned out to be a lie...

237
00:21:33,251 --> 00:21:37,005
does that also mean
his whole identity is a lie?

238
00:21:43,094 --> 00:21:46,014
Attorney, a lie is a lie.

239
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:49,559
You knew,
so you should pay for it as well.

240
00:22:06,367 --> 00:22:09,120
<i>Good day. May I ask you something?</i>

241
00:22:10,621 --> 00:22:12,957
<i>I am looking for someone.</i>

242
00:22:13,750 --> 00:22:15,918
Have you seen this woman
pass by here?

243
00:22:17,086 --> 00:22:18,087
No.

244
00:22:18,796 --> 00:22:20,298
Are you sure?

245
00:22:51,829 --> 00:22:52,789
No, sir.

246
00:22:52,872 --> 00:22:54,540
All right. Thank you.

247
00:22:54,624 --> 00:22:56,626
- Okay, then.
- Excuse me.

248
00:22:56,918 --> 00:22:58,586
May I ask you something?

249
00:22:58,669 --> 00:22:59,921
It's just that...

250
00:23:00,296 --> 00:23:02,048
I'm looking for this woman.

251
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:05,468
She was just here earlier.

252
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:08,721
- Where did she go?
- She went in that direction.

253
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:11,390
- Yes, that way.
- Thank you!

254
00:24:08,030 --> 00:24:10,032
<i>We will be better as parents.</i>

255
00:24:20,501 --> 00:24:21,919
<i>Are you there?</i>

256
00:24:23,421 --> 00:24:25,506
<i>Are you really there, my child?</i>

257
00:24:30,970 --> 00:24:34,891
<i>My child...</i>
<i>What am I going to do with you?</i>

258
00:24:40,271 --> 00:24:43,524
<i>I don't even know what to do with myself.</i>

259
00:24:52,074 --> 00:24:54,577
<i>I'm sorry,</i>
<i>we're not ready for you.</i>

260
00:24:57,371 --> 00:24:58,414
Ana!

261
00:25:01,584 --> 00:25:02,585
Ana!

262
00:25:23,356 --> 00:25:25,524
Even if you report us to the cops...

263
00:25:26,108 --> 00:25:27,610
nothing will happen.

264
00:25:28,361 --> 00:25:31,572
Boss Eric can just as easily
abduct you again.

265
00:25:31,656 --> 00:25:32,490
Look at me!

266
00:25:34,492 --> 00:25:35,660
Remember this.

267
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:39,413
You may be free now,
but we still have eyes on you.

268
00:25:39,497 --> 00:25:41,082
Now, get lost!

269
00:25:42,833 --> 00:25:44,001
Go!

270
00:25:48,089 --> 00:25:49,340
Take off your clothes.

271
00:25:57,181 --> 00:25:58,432
What are you waiting for?

272
00:26:06,899 --> 00:26:08,818
Take it off!

273
00:26:21,664 --> 00:26:23,582
Hey, any updates?

274
00:26:23,666 --> 00:26:25,584
<i>We already let Angel out.</i>

275
00:26:25,668 --> 00:26:26,919
<i>She's out already.</i>

276
00:26:28,504 --> 00:26:29,672
Okay.

277
00:26:30,798 --> 00:26:32,300
You heard him, right?

278
00:26:32,758 --> 00:26:33,843
Thanks, man.

279
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:39,765
Go and call your friend.

280
00:26:39,849 --> 00:26:41,017
Wait!

281
00:26:41,100 --> 00:26:44,520
I haven't... I haven't
seen her yet. I need to check.

282
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:46,230
Besides, wouldn't--

283
00:26:46,314 --> 00:26:48,316
Call her now!

284
00:26:48,399 --> 00:26:52,069
You know, if she's not coming...

285
00:26:52,153 --> 00:26:53,988
I'll just have you instead.

286
00:26:54,071 --> 00:26:55,698
She's on her way now!

287
00:26:55,781 --> 00:26:58,534
Hey, hey, hey! I did you a favor already.

288
00:26:59,035 --> 00:27:01,704
Your friend is now free! So now...

289
00:27:02,705 --> 00:27:04,790
it's your turn to do me a favor!

290
00:27:05,207 --> 00:27:06,917
No! Help!

291
00:27:07,001 --> 00:27:09,587
Bridgette! Hold on, girl!

292
00:27:09,670 --> 00:27:14,216
Please stay strong, girl! We're close!

293
00:27:14,300 --> 00:27:19,138
Come here!

294
00:27:20,348 --> 00:27:23,934
- Carlota! Help me!

295
00:27:24,018 --> 00:27:26,103
Help me!

296
00:27:26,187 --> 00:27:30,274
Please stop!

297
00:27:30,358 --> 00:27:33,652
Help me! Help, please!

298
00:27:33,736 --> 00:27:35,237
Put your hands up!

299
00:27:39,075 --> 00:27:40,910
Stop what you're doing!

300
00:27:40,993 --> 00:27:42,828
- Bridge!
- Carlota!

301
00:27:42,912 --> 00:27:44,914
- What's going on?
- Put your hands up!

302
00:27:58,010 --> 00:28:01,680
Shh!

303
00:28:04,392 --> 00:28:06,977
- It's me.
- Diane?

304
00:28:07,061 --> 00:28:09,647
- Okay? It's me.
- Diane...

305
00:28:12,024 --> 00:28:14,026
Diane...

306
00:28:17,279 --> 00:28:19,782
Shh. Don't cry anymore.

307
00:28:19,865 --> 00:28:21,909
- How did you find me?
- You're safe now.

308
00:28:21,992 --> 00:28:23,411
- They're following me!
- No.

309
00:28:23,494 --> 00:28:26,288
- I'm right here. I'm here.
- They're following me.

310
00:28:26,372 --> 00:28:27,581
Come, let's go.

311
00:28:43,222 --> 00:28:44,306
Miss.

312
00:28:44,390 --> 00:28:47,810
Miss, is he Brian Robles?

313
00:28:47,893 --> 00:28:49,562
Yes.

314
00:28:49,645 --> 00:28:52,565
He's my brother.

315
00:28:54,733 --> 00:28:58,571
Brian!

316
00:29:00,573 --> 00:29:01,740
Ana!

317
00:29:07,163 --> 00:29:08,998
What are you doing here?

318
00:29:10,708 --> 00:29:12,460
How did you know that I was here?

319
00:29:12,543 --> 00:29:14,879
Ana, I asked so many people!

320
00:29:15,880 --> 00:29:17,882
I was so worried about you.

321
00:29:17,965 --> 00:29:20,050
Luckily, someone saw you.

322
00:29:21,635 --> 00:29:23,888
What's happening?
Why didn't you attend the wedding?

323
00:29:25,222 --> 00:29:26,640
I just didn't want to.

324
00:29:30,561 --> 00:29:31,645
Ana...

325
00:29:33,022 --> 00:29:36,108
you would kill if there was something
wrong with your clients' clothes.

326
00:29:38,152 --> 00:29:40,070
This has never happened before.

327
00:29:41,071 --> 00:29:42,490
People change.

328
00:29:45,409 --> 00:29:48,829
Ana, can you tell me
what's happening, please? Please.

329
00:29:49,497 --> 00:29:52,416
A spouse
doesn't have to know everything, right?

330
00:29:52,500 --> 00:29:54,210
No, I think... I think this one...

331
00:29:54,293 --> 00:29:56,670
you have to tell me
why you're here and what's going on.

332
00:29:56,754 --> 00:29:58,005
I'm worried about you.

333
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:03,219
So, there are things
that we should and shouldn't know,

334
00:30:03,302 --> 00:30:05,346
and you're the one who gets to decide?

335
00:30:09,016 --> 00:30:10,518
Is this about me?

336
00:30:13,687 --> 00:30:15,940
It's always about you, love.

337
00:30:17,900 --> 00:30:22,154
Everything... is about you.

338
00:30:23,948 --> 00:30:25,157
Ana...

339
00:30:25,241 --> 00:30:26,867
Ana! Ana?

340
00:30:26,951 --> 00:30:29,286
Ana, what's happening? Ana?

341
00:30:32,081 --> 00:30:33,207
Tell everyone

342
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:35,292
that we'll have
a large-scale search operation on the sea.

343
00:30:35,376 --> 00:30:37,294
- Sir?
- Yes.

344
00:30:37,378 --> 00:30:40,256
We'll do it in the area
where Brian Robles's body was found.

345
00:30:40,339 --> 00:30:44,009
We'll gather all the clues
related to the case, okay?

346
00:30:44,093 --> 00:30:46,762
- Okay.
- Okay, go! Hurry up.

347
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:14,206
You're pregnant?

348
00:31:19,753 --> 00:31:22,172
How are you feeling, Ana?

349
00:31:22,965 --> 00:31:24,633
Ana, I'm so happy.

350
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:28,387
You're pregnant.

351
00:31:34,059 --> 00:31:35,269
Why now?

352
00:31:39,565 --> 00:31:42,067
There were a lot of chances before.

353
00:31:44,570 --> 00:31:46,739
Why did I have to be pregnant now?

354
00:31:49,867 --> 00:31:51,118
It's okay.

355
00:31:52,328 --> 00:31:54,913
How can we be good parents

356
00:31:54,997 --> 00:31:57,583
when we don't even have a good marriage?

357
00:32:02,087 --> 00:32:03,255
Fine.

358
00:32:04,131 --> 00:32:06,884
Maybe it's just right
that I became pregnant right now.

359
00:32:07,926 --> 00:32:12,264
So my child would grow up knowing
how big a liar their father is.

360
00:32:14,725 --> 00:32:16,143
Ana. Ana!

361
00:32:16,727 --> 00:32:20,356
Ana, please stop!
Ana! Ana, stop!

362
00:32:20,439 --> 00:32:23,108
What you're doing will affect our child!

363
00:32:23,651 --> 00:32:25,653
- Ana!
- And what about you?

364
00:32:25,736 --> 00:32:27,905
Do you think
that will not affect our child?

365
00:32:27,988 --> 00:32:28,989
What have I done?

366
00:32:29,073 --> 00:32:30,324
You lie!

367
00:32:31,158 --> 00:32:34,411
You lie and you lie every single time!

368
00:32:35,913 --> 00:32:39,750
You're not a real lawyer!
You're just pretending to be one!

369
00:32:40,876 --> 00:32:42,044
What?

370
00:32:42,127 --> 00:32:44,713
Oh, come on, just stop! Stop!

371
00:32:44,797 --> 00:32:47,675
Nobody can hear you!
It's just us here!

372
00:32:47,758 --> 00:32:49,927
Are you still going to lie to me?

373
00:32:51,387 --> 00:32:54,890
Ben... just be honest.

374
00:32:55,974 --> 00:32:58,102
You didn't pass the bar.

375
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:00,562
You didn't graduate.

376
00:33:00,646 --> 00:33:02,731
I saw your yearbook!

377
00:33:02,815 --> 00:33:05,234
I checked your IBP number.

378
00:33:07,611 --> 00:33:08,779
Ben...

379
00:33:10,114 --> 00:33:12,616
you're a fraud!

380
00:33:14,201 --> 00:33:16,453
But here you are in Vallente...

381
00:33:16,537 --> 00:33:19,623
it's like you're this superhero lawyer!

382
00:33:26,422 --> 00:33:32,928
I can't believe
I thought I was going crazy!

383
00:33:33,011 --> 00:33:36,682
I thought my suspicions were wrong.

384
00:33:36,765 --> 00:33:38,434
But it's you!

385
00:33:38,517 --> 00:33:40,853
You fooled me!

386
00:33:42,980 --> 00:33:44,732
Who are you?

387
00:33:46,483 --> 00:33:47,818
Who are you?

388
00:33:47,901 --> 00:33:50,696
Who are you?
I don't even know who you are!

389
00:33:50,779 --> 00:33:53,115
- Who are you, huh? Who are you?
- Ana, stop.

390
00:33:53,198 --> 00:33:56,285
- Who are you?
- Ana, stop. Ana, stop.

391
00:33:56,869 --> 00:33:59,204
Okay! Okay. Okay.

392
00:34:06,837 --> 00:34:08,005
It's true.

393
00:34:15,429 --> 00:34:16,764
But Ana...

394
00:34:18,557 --> 00:34:20,309
I defended the weak.

395
00:34:22,895 --> 00:34:26,315
I championed for those
who can't fight just because they're poor.

396
00:34:28,025 --> 00:34:29,777
I served the farmers.

397
00:34:30,778 --> 00:34:34,865
Ana, I've built a company
that will support and defend them.

398
00:34:37,367 --> 00:34:39,453
I'm a better lawyer than others.

399
00:34:39,536 --> 00:34:41,038
No, that doesn't make it right.

400
00:34:41,121 --> 00:34:43,040
Okay, I went to law school!

401
00:34:43,123 --> 00:34:45,626
I went to law school,
but I couldn't take the bar.

402
00:34:47,211 --> 00:34:49,546
Because I was charged with fraud.

403
00:34:50,297 --> 00:34:54,384
I was involved
in something that dealt with money.

404
00:34:55,010 --> 00:34:57,513
In short, I did not graduate.

405
00:34:57,596 --> 00:35:00,349
So I had to use
another person's credentials

406
00:35:00,432 --> 00:35:02,434
just so I can keep going.

407
00:35:04,436 --> 00:35:06,438
'Cause I had Regina.

408
00:35:06,522 --> 00:35:09,691
I wanted to continue caring for Regina.

409
00:35:10,150 --> 00:35:11,401
And I had a dream.

410
00:35:12,319 --> 00:35:14,571
And my dream was to become a lawyer.

411
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:17,950
Just so we could have a fighting chance.

412
00:35:19,701 --> 00:35:21,203
That's it, Ana.

413
00:35:21,703 --> 00:35:24,790
That's why I did what I did.

414
00:35:28,961 --> 00:35:30,712
You used me?

415
00:35:39,221 --> 00:35:41,390
Did you really love me, Ben?

416
00:35:43,809 --> 00:35:47,312
Or did you just use me
to legitimize your life?

417
00:35:50,065 --> 00:35:51,400
Ana, listen.

418
00:35:53,485 --> 00:35:55,654
I love you so much.

419
00:35:57,197 --> 00:35:59,366
I love you so much, Ana.

420
00:36:01,535 --> 00:36:04,705
My love for you has no lies.

421
00:36:06,665 --> 00:36:09,334
How? How can I believe that

422
00:36:09,418 --> 00:36:12,087
when I can't trust anything about you?

423
00:36:16,008 --> 00:36:17,259
I can't do this.

424
00:36:17,342 --> 00:36:18,260
I'm done.

425
00:36:18,343 --> 00:36:21,597
Wait.
Just because I'm not a real lawyer?

426
00:36:22,472 --> 00:36:27,060
Because you... betrayed me.

427
00:36:29,146 --> 00:36:32,566
And now that
you've dragged me into all of your lies,

428
00:36:32,649 --> 00:36:35,068
I need to do something to correct them.

429
00:36:55,339 --> 00:36:57,090
Okay, let's go.

430
00:37:09,811 --> 00:37:12,064
Are you sure you're all right?

431
00:37:14,983 --> 00:37:17,319
How is Angel doing?

432
00:37:17,402 --> 00:37:19,237
She's getting better.

433
00:37:20,530 --> 00:37:22,616
I took her to her mother.

434
00:37:22,699 --> 00:37:26,286
She'll message us when she's all settled.

435
00:37:30,582 --> 00:37:32,501
Girl, hey.

436
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:35,963
It's all okay now. We're all okay.

437
00:37:39,716 --> 00:37:40,884
Here.

438
00:37:52,479 --> 00:37:55,482
You're right.
What matters is...

439
00:37:55,565 --> 00:37:57,150
Angel's now safe.

440
00:37:58,652 --> 00:38:00,153
And so are you.

441
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:03,782
We're all together again.

442
00:38:08,120 --> 00:38:11,289
We're still not complete.
Beth's not with us yet.

443
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:15,544
Diane,
what did you and Beth last talk about?

444
00:38:20,465 --> 00:38:23,301
The last thing she told me
was that she was coming home.

445
00:38:25,595 --> 00:38:30,100
I talked with Megan earlier.
She said Beth still hasn't contacted them.

446
00:38:32,936 --> 00:38:37,107
We just wrapped up one problem,
now here comes another one.

447
00:38:41,028 --> 00:38:42,696
Now, it's Beth.

448
00:38:44,531 --> 00:38:46,116
I'm sorry, but...

449
00:38:46,783 --> 00:38:48,952
I have a bad feeling about this.

450
00:38:57,294 --> 00:39:01,048
Go and move the second body now.
Take it to the morgue.

451
00:39:01,923 --> 00:39:03,341
Sir! Sir!

452
00:39:03,425 --> 00:39:04,843
They found another body!

453
00:39:08,764 --> 00:39:11,850
- That's already the third one.
- It is, sir.

454
00:39:15,937 --> 00:39:18,356
How many more bodies
did they throw into the sea?

455
00:39:33,246 --> 00:39:36,166
<i>Hi, Ana. Sorry, I look tired.</i>

456
00:39:36,249 --> 00:39:40,128
<i>But look at this place.</i>
<i>Look at that place.</i>

457
00:39:40,212 --> 00:39:41,463
Look at this.

458
00:39:44,257 --> 00:39:48,261
So this could be your receiving area
for your clients.

459
00:39:50,097 --> 00:39:51,264
And then...

460
00:39:52,265 --> 00:39:53,350
here.

461
00:39:54,935 --> 00:39:57,104
This... this one...

462
00:39:57,813 --> 00:40:00,565
This one will be your workshop.

463
00:40:03,652 --> 00:40:04,736
<i>And...</i>

464
00:40:05,695 --> 00:40:07,489
<i>the master's bedroom.</i>

465
00:40:08,448 --> 00:40:10,450
<i>There's a room next to it.</i>

466
00:40:11,326 --> 00:40:13,662
<i>Now that could be the baby's room.</i>

467
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:29,010
Wow.

468
00:40:29,886 --> 00:40:32,973
That man's effort as a husband...

469
00:40:35,016 --> 00:40:37,769
Are you really siding with him, Ma?

470
00:40:37,853 --> 00:40:40,105
He lied.

471
00:40:40,856 --> 00:40:43,942
Why, Silvana?
Are you perfect?

472
00:40:44,359 --> 00:40:46,611
Have you never lied in your life

473
00:40:46,695 --> 00:40:51,032
to demand a hundred percent honesty
from your husband?

474
00:40:51,575 --> 00:40:55,162
Silvana... he did that out of love.

475
00:40:55,245 --> 00:40:59,875
Why is it so easy for you to say
he lied out of love?

476
00:40:59,958 --> 00:41:02,460
How can it be love if there are lies?

477
00:41:03,253 --> 00:41:06,006
Ana, we don't live in a perfect world.

478
00:41:06,089 --> 00:41:09,759
There can never be
complete honesty in a relationship.

479
00:41:09,843 --> 00:41:13,847
Yeah, but you make it sound like
what Ben did wasn't a big deal.

480
00:41:14,723 --> 00:41:16,641
That's eight years, Ma.

481
00:41:17,267 --> 00:41:20,353
He hid that from me for eight long years.

482
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:24,733
He fooled people for nearly a decade...

483
00:41:24,816 --> 00:41:26,484
by posing as a lawyer.

484
00:41:27,027 --> 00:41:29,613
So what if he isn't a lawyer?

485
00:41:30,822 --> 00:41:32,991
He did a better job
protecting other people...

486
00:41:33,074 --> 00:41:37,370
than actual lawyers
who are either stupid or corrupt.

487
00:41:37,454 --> 00:41:40,624
No, the end does not justify the means.

488
00:41:40,707 --> 00:41:43,543
It's a noble deception, Silvana.

489
00:41:44,502 --> 00:41:48,673
When has lying been a good thing?

490
00:41:48,757 --> 00:41:50,842
You should know, Ma.

491
00:41:50,926 --> 00:41:55,013
Weren't you furious at Papa
when he betrayed you?

492
00:41:55,639 --> 00:41:58,475
He left me for another woman.

493
00:41:58,558 --> 00:42:00,227
That's completely different!

494
00:42:00,310 --> 00:42:03,396
No. They're the same.

495
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:06,733
They lied about different things,
but they still lied.

496
00:42:07,776 --> 00:42:10,403
Look, Ana,
all I'm saying is that...

497
00:42:10,487 --> 00:42:14,241
he did it all out of love. Okay?

498
00:42:14,324 --> 00:42:17,452
Ma, listen to yourself.

499
00:42:20,163 --> 00:42:23,166
I'm not saying what he did was right.

500
00:42:23,250 --> 00:42:25,669
But your husband truly loves you.

501
00:42:26,544 --> 00:42:31,299
Not everyone experiences
that kind of love.

502
00:42:31,841 --> 00:42:33,927
Did he hurt you?

503
00:42:34,010 --> 00:42:35,512
Did he ever lay a hand on you?

504
00:42:35,929 --> 00:42:37,514
He didn't, right?

505
00:42:45,105 --> 00:42:49,276
What kind of life will my child have?

506
00:42:51,278 --> 00:42:54,781
You and Ben can still give your child
a good life...

507
00:42:55,407 --> 00:42:58,076
if you guys will stay together.

508
00:42:59,995 --> 00:43:01,079
No!

509
00:43:02,455 --> 00:43:06,793
No.
I can't stomach what Ben did.

510
00:43:06,876 --> 00:43:07,961
Okay, Silvana.

511
00:43:08,878 --> 00:43:10,547
What do you want to do?

512
00:43:11,214 --> 00:43:13,383
You want to leave him?

513
00:43:14,467 --> 00:43:15,635
Look, Ana.

514
00:43:16,344 --> 00:43:19,264
If you can wholeheartedly tell me...

515
00:43:19,347 --> 00:43:22,684
that your life
would be better without Ben,

516
00:43:22,767 --> 00:43:24,978
that you'll be happier without him...

517
00:43:25,061 --> 00:43:27,647
then by all means, go! Leave!

518
00:43:28,565 --> 00:43:30,567
But if not...

519
00:43:30,650 --> 00:43:33,653
please, think twice.

520
00:43:34,070 --> 00:43:35,488
Thrice!

521
00:43:36,781 --> 00:43:39,200
I don't know what to do...

522
00:43:45,081 --> 00:43:48,376
This is wrong.
This is wrong.

523
00:43:50,462 --> 00:43:53,465
What's the point of doing what's right

524
00:43:53,548 --> 00:43:55,800
if your life is miserable?

525
00:44:17,447 --> 00:44:20,200
One victim suffered head trauma,

526
00:44:20,283 --> 00:44:23,328
while the other two had
slash wounds to the neck.

527
00:44:23,411 --> 00:44:25,080
All of the victims were wrapped

528
00:44:25,163 --> 00:44:28,249
and the knots used to bind them
were identical.

529
00:44:28,333 --> 00:44:31,586
So there is a pattern. It's possible
that the same person killed them all.

530
00:44:46,309 --> 00:44:49,479
Oh, Ana.
What brings you here?

531
00:44:50,814 --> 00:44:52,565
Did something happen?

532
00:44:53,441 --> 00:44:56,194
You need to know something about Ben.

533
00:44:58,363 --> 00:45:00,782
Please don't tell me it's another scandal.

534
00:45:00,865 --> 00:45:03,493
The issue with his sister
hasn't even blown over yet.

535
00:45:03,576 --> 00:45:06,079
That's just one of his lies.

536
00:45:06,162 --> 00:45:09,290
What are you saying?
Did Ben hurt you?

537
00:45:10,959 --> 00:45:12,460
He's a fraud.

538
00:45:13,336 --> 00:45:16,589
He's not a real lawyer.
He's a fake!

539
00:45:27,267 --> 00:45:28,768
<i>Before he arrived at Vallente,</i>

540
00:45:28,852 --> 00:45:30,937
<i>he was already pretending to be a lawyer.</i>

541
00:45:32,730 --> 00:45:34,649
This is for everyone's sake.

542
00:45:36,276 --> 00:45:38,611
I represented you
in these contracts and cases...

543
00:45:38,695 --> 00:45:40,488
that I won for you.

544
00:45:40,572 --> 00:45:45,743
Now, when they find out
I'm not really a lawyer,

545
00:45:45,827 --> 00:45:47,912
it will affect all of this.

546
00:45:49,539 --> 00:45:52,542
You've got some nerve
putting us in this situation.

547
00:45:52,625 --> 00:45:54,794
We trusted you.

548
00:45:54,878 --> 00:45:57,005
And I delivered, didn't I, sir?

549
00:45:58,214 --> 00:46:01,301
I don't know
where this arrogance comes from.

550
00:46:03,344 --> 00:46:07,015
If I planned
to rob you of money and power,

551
00:46:07,891 --> 00:46:11,561
I never would've told you the truth.

552
00:46:12,645 --> 00:46:14,814
I would've turned my back on you
a long time ago.

553
00:46:15,982 --> 00:46:18,401
I've been very loyal.

554
00:46:20,278 --> 00:46:21,946
And I expect the same.

555
00:46:22,822 --> 00:46:25,241
Mariano.

556
00:46:25,867 --> 00:46:28,119
Our reputation is on the line!

557
00:46:29,496 --> 00:46:30,747
You heard the man.

558
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:32,248
Enough, Mona.

559
00:46:34,751 --> 00:46:36,169
Good job, Ben.

560
00:46:39,589 --> 00:46:40,840
Wait.

561
00:46:45,303 --> 00:46:46,804
You knew all along?

562
00:46:49,182 --> 00:46:53,019
No. This is new information.

563
00:46:53,102 --> 00:46:55,605
But to be honest, so what?

564
00:46:55,688 --> 00:46:59,359
I mean, everything he does
is for the good of the <i>azucarera.</i>

565
00:47:00,235 --> 00:47:01,277
What?

566
00:47:02,111 --> 00:47:04,280
You're just going to let this slide?

567
00:47:05,073 --> 00:47:06,824
- Auntie!
- My dear...

568
00:47:06,908 --> 00:47:09,994
sometimes,
technicalities don't really matter.

569
00:47:10,078 --> 00:47:12,372
Especially if you look at the big picture.

570
00:47:13,039 --> 00:47:15,291
Wha-- What big picture?

571
00:47:15,375 --> 00:47:18,253
They'd have to reopen
cases he won for the <i>azucarera.</i>

572
00:47:18,336 --> 00:47:20,338
Including ownership of the land...

573
00:47:20,421 --> 00:47:23,091
that took years to fight in court.

574
00:47:23,883 --> 00:47:25,218
We can't afford that.

575
00:47:27,470 --> 00:47:29,472
I know it's hard to accept.

576
00:47:29,556 --> 00:47:31,391
Especially you're his wife.

577
00:47:32,016 --> 00:47:33,351
But please...

578
00:47:33,434 --> 00:47:35,103
don't tell anyone about this.

579
00:47:39,190 --> 00:47:40,275
What?

580
00:47:41,109 --> 00:47:44,696
This is all for the best. For all of us.

581
00:47:45,446 --> 00:47:47,282
Do you understand me?

582
00:48:16,019 --> 00:48:18,104
- Ana, I'm--
- No, no.

583
00:48:18,187 --> 00:48:21,190
You scheming bastard.

584
00:48:22,442 --> 00:48:23,776
You planned everything.

585
00:48:24,360 --> 00:48:28,031
You even got the Saguils involved
in your lies.

586
00:48:28,114 --> 00:48:30,533
And you want me to believe...

587
00:48:31,200 --> 00:48:33,119
that you didn't use me?

588
00:48:33,202 --> 00:48:37,540
Oh, my God.
Ana, I'm not using you.

589
00:48:38,625 --> 00:48:40,209
I swear.

590
00:48:42,211 --> 00:48:43,963
- Ana--
- No, don't touch me!

591
00:48:48,843 --> 00:48:50,762
You're full of lies.

592
00:48:52,388 --> 00:48:53,473
Don't follow me.

593
00:48:53,556 --> 00:48:55,183
Ana, Ana-- Please.

594
00:48:55,266 --> 00:48:57,101
Ana. Ana!

595
00:48:58,645 --> 00:49:01,648
Ana. Ana, please.

596
00:49:06,194 --> 00:49:08,863
We'll have a hard time
identifying the victims.

597
00:49:10,448 --> 00:49:13,117
They were submerged in water for too long.

598
00:49:13,701 --> 00:49:15,453
What are we going to do, sir?

599
00:49:17,830 --> 00:49:21,167
We can compare them
against the missing persons list.

600
00:49:22,168 --> 00:49:24,587
Maybe we can find a match
based on their height

601
00:49:24,671 --> 00:49:28,091
or other identifying features
that could give us a lead.

602
00:49:29,967 --> 00:49:32,553
This one has tattoos.

603
00:49:33,846 --> 00:49:35,181
This one too.

604
00:49:36,808 --> 00:49:38,726
I don't know, sir.

605
00:49:39,936 --> 00:49:41,688
Are tattoos our only lead?

606
00:49:41,771 --> 00:49:44,107
No.
We have to start somewhere.

607
00:49:44,190 --> 00:49:46,818
I know it's hard,
but we have to figure this out.

608
00:49:46,901 --> 00:49:50,071
We don't know if we're dealing
with one person or a group.

609
00:49:50,154 --> 00:49:53,157
We need to make sure
there won't be any more victims.

610
00:49:54,784 --> 00:49:56,035
Copy, sir.

611
00:50:05,211 --> 00:50:07,714
When was the last time you saw Beth?

612
00:50:10,717 --> 00:50:13,136
On the day of her flight to Manila.

613
00:50:13,219 --> 00:50:15,555
She was moving out her stuff.

614
00:50:16,347 --> 00:50:17,765
What did she tell you?

615
00:50:17,849 --> 00:50:20,393
Did she recommend this apartment to you?

616
00:50:21,936 --> 00:50:23,146
Ah, yes.

617
00:50:23,229 --> 00:50:25,732
She told me that
since she was going home already,

618
00:50:25,815 --> 00:50:28,609
I could take over the lease.

619
00:50:28,693 --> 00:50:33,114
Even though you're friends with Beth,
you can't use her deposit.

620
00:50:34,282 --> 00:50:35,616
What deposit?

621
00:50:36,701 --> 00:50:40,955
Yes. Didn't she tell you
that she still has a month's deposit?

622
00:50:42,081 --> 00:50:44,083
Well, I can't blame her.

623
00:50:44,167 --> 00:50:47,587
If I were in her shoes,
I'd also get out of here.

624
00:50:52,508 --> 00:50:54,927
Why? What happened to Beth?

625
00:50:55,011 --> 00:50:59,140
She doesn't really talk
about her personal life.

626
00:50:59,640 --> 00:51:03,728
Rumor has it,
it's because of Doña Imelda's doing.

627
00:51:06,397 --> 00:51:08,232
Doña Imelda?

628
00:51:09,484 --> 00:51:12,570
Hold on, Ana.
Why do you insist on driving yourself?

629
00:51:12,653 --> 00:51:14,155
We have a driver!

630
00:51:14,238 --> 00:51:17,158
Ma, if you don't want to come with me
to my OB-GYN appointment, it's okay.

631
00:51:17,241 --> 00:51:18,367
I can go by myself.

632
00:51:18,451 --> 00:51:20,119
Nonsense.
I'm already dressed up.

633
00:51:20,203 --> 00:51:22,497
Come on, come on. Let's go, let's go.

634
00:51:22,580 --> 00:51:23,956
- My goodness.
- Ma'am?

635
00:51:24,040 --> 00:51:26,918
- What?
- Someone's here for Miss Ana.

636
00:51:27,001 --> 00:51:27,919
Is it Ben?

637
00:51:28,002 --> 00:51:29,295
No, ma'am.

638
00:51:29,378 --> 00:51:31,047
It's her.

639
00:51:36,761 --> 00:51:39,764
Cedes, you're not supposed to tell anyone
where my daughter is.

640
00:51:39,847 --> 00:51:42,517
She doesn't want to be found!
What were you thinking?

641
00:51:44,435 --> 00:51:46,771
Tell me what you need.

642
00:51:46,854 --> 00:51:48,356
We're worried about Beth.

643
00:51:48,439 --> 00:51:50,983
Her siblings and I can't reach her.

644
00:51:51,067 --> 00:51:53,486
And you think I know where she is?

645
00:51:54,028 --> 00:51:56,781
You and your friends are unbelievable.

646
00:51:56,864 --> 00:51:59,867
You might know where she is
because of what happened.

647
00:52:00,535 --> 00:52:01,953
Yes, I know about that.

648
00:52:02,036 --> 00:52:03,955
And I also know the rumors going around

649
00:52:04,038 --> 00:52:06,749
that your mother did something
to my friend.

650
00:52:06,833 --> 00:52:09,335
And now you're going after my mom?

651
00:52:09,877 --> 00:52:13,798
If you knew what really happened,
you wouldn't have come here.

652
00:52:13,881 --> 00:52:15,925
I was humiliated.

653
00:52:16,008 --> 00:52:18,135
She caused so much trouble.

654
00:52:18,219 --> 00:52:20,680
Which is why I had no choice
but to come here.

655
00:52:20,763 --> 00:52:23,349
My friend's a nobody.

656
00:52:23,432 --> 00:52:27,228
Who knows what you could've done to her
because of her foolishness?

657
00:52:27,311 --> 00:52:31,399
Beth means nothing to me now, okay?

658
00:52:37,780 --> 00:52:39,949
If you won't tell me where she is,

659
00:52:40,908 --> 00:52:42,743
I'll have to talk to Attorney Ben.

660
00:52:42,827 --> 00:52:45,705
Then ask him.
I don't know where he is.

661
00:52:46,998 --> 00:52:48,082
Huh?

662
00:52:49,208 --> 00:52:50,835
You're not together anymore?

663
00:52:51,669 --> 00:52:52,837
Is that all you need?

664
00:52:53,588 --> 00:52:56,090
You may go now. I have somewhere to be.

665
00:53:10,104 --> 00:53:13,274
Those CCTV cameras don't work?

666
00:53:13,357 --> 00:53:15,943
No, sir. They've been broken for a while.

667
00:53:17,361 --> 00:53:20,948
Do you have a list of clients
who use these yachts?

668
00:53:21,032 --> 00:53:24,535
We do, sir. But we don't have records
for all passengers.

669
00:53:24,619 --> 00:53:26,829
We only have records of those they report.

670
00:53:26,913 --> 00:53:27,830
Okay.

671
00:53:27,914 --> 00:53:31,083
We're checking areas accessible by boat.

672
00:53:32,126 --> 00:53:35,880
Have any yacht owners
been acting suspiciously?

673
00:53:36,547 --> 00:53:38,799
We have a lot of shady clients, sir.

674
00:53:38,883 --> 00:53:40,551
These are rich folks we're talking about.

675
00:53:40,635 --> 00:53:43,804
They bring all kinds of people here.

676
00:53:44,472 --> 00:53:46,140
Like who?

677
00:53:46,223 --> 00:53:47,725
Uh... women, sir.

678
00:53:47,808 --> 00:53:51,479
This yacht is owned by a doctor.

679
00:53:51,562 --> 00:53:55,149
That's where he performs his "procedures."

680
00:53:58,194 --> 00:54:00,947
What about this one?
What's this one hiding?

681
00:54:01,030 --> 00:54:04,075
Nothing, sir.
That's Attorney Ben's boat.

682
00:54:05,576 --> 00:54:08,162
Attorney Ben? Ben Santos?

683
00:54:08,245 --> 00:54:10,164
Yes, Ben Santos. Spotless, right?

684
00:54:10,247 --> 00:54:13,626
Only Attorney Ben
keeps his yacht this clean.

685
00:54:13,709 --> 00:54:17,046
But he's not here often.

686
00:54:30,810 --> 00:54:34,480
<i> Fear has swept</i>
<i>the town of Vallente...</i>

687
00:54:34,563 --> 00:54:36,190
- What is going on?
<i>- ...as bodies were found</i>

688
00:54:36,273 --> 00:54:38,109
<i>- in the last few days.</i>
- Nanny?

689
00:54:38,192 --> 00:54:41,070
- Nanny, water, please.
- Okay, ma'am.

690
00:54:41,153 --> 00:54:42,905
<i>Authorities recovered the bodies</i>

691
00:54:42,989 --> 00:54:46,367
<i>after divers found them at sea.</i>

692
00:54:52,832 --> 00:54:54,917
That's a lot of bodies!

693
00:54:55,001 --> 00:54:57,503
What's happening to Vallente?

694
00:54:57,586 --> 00:54:59,046
That dock is nearby!

695
00:54:59,130 --> 00:55:02,967
<i>A relative has identified</i>
<i>the body of Brian Robles.</i>

696
00:55:08,180 --> 00:55:09,348
<i>So far,</i>

697
00:55:09,432 --> 00:55:11,934
<i>three bodies have been recovered</i>
<i>by the police.</i>

698
00:55:12,643 --> 00:55:16,814
<i>Relatives have identified</i>
<i>the remains of the victims.</i>

699
00:55:16,897 --> 00:55:21,318
<i>They have been identified</i>
<i>as Danny Pascual and Joel Geraldo.</i>

700
00:55:25,239 --> 00:55:28,576
<i>The police are doing everything we can</i>

701
00:55:28,659 --> 00:55:30,995
<i>to help the victims' relatives.</i>

702
00:55:31,078 --> 00:55:33,456
<i>An investigation is underway to determine</i>

703
00:55:33,539 --> 00:55:36,125
<i>if there's a connection</i>
<i>between the victims' deaths.</i>

704
00:55:36,208 --> 00:55:38,627
<i>We have not ruled out the possibility</i>

705
00:55:38,711 --> 00:55:42,715
<i>that a group or an individual</i>
<i>is behind these crimes.</i>

706
00:55:44,091 --> 00:55:46,093
Ma'am, here's your water.

707
00:55:59,106 --> 00:56:00,691
<i>Brian is gone, Ana.</i>

708
00:56:01,233 --> 00:56:03,778
- Ben!
- <i>No, I just saw Brian.</i>

709
00:56:03,861 --> 00:56:05,696
- <i>He stopped by our house.</i>
- Ana.

710
00:56:05,780 --> 00:56:08,365
<i>- He's going through something.</i>
- <i>No, he's not.</i>

711
00:56:08,699 --> 00:56:10,618
<i>Ben's money is all he's after.</i>

712
00:56:10,701 --> 00:56:13,287
Miss Ana, someone's looking for you.

713
00:56:13,746 --> 00:56:16,499
- Oh.
- Miss Ana Madrigal-Santos?

714
00:56:16,582 --> 00:56:17,583
Yes.

715
00:56:17,666 --> 00:56:19,919
Danny Pascual from DPEvents.

716
00:56:20,294 --> 00:56:21,629
Hello, how can I help you?

717
00:56:21,712 --> 00:56:23,923
Hi, could I interview you
about your husband?

718
00:56:24,006 --> 00:56:26,092
It's for the Saguils' event.

719
00:56:26,175 --> 00:56:28,636
Ben killed my husband.
Ben killed my husband.

720
00:56:28,719 --> 00:56:29,637
Regina!

721
00:56:29,720 --> 00:56:31,764
<i>With how long</i>
<i>I've been looking after Regina,</i>

722
00:56:31,847 --> 00:56:33,599
<i>- she's told me a lot...</i>
- Did you see it?

723
00:56:33,682 --> 00:56:34,934
<i>...about the things</i>
<i>Ben does to other people.</i>

724
00:56:35,017 --> 00:56:36,143
No.

725
00:56:36,227 --> 00:56:37,520
But I know he did it.

726
00:56:39,688 --> 00:56:42,358
<i>Have I told you</i>
<i>it's not just Joel that he killed?</i>

727
00:56:42,441 --> 00:56:45,444
<i>He killed Papa too.</i>
<i>I saw it with my own eyes.</i>

728
00:56:48,614 --> 00:56:50,407
We're worried about Beth.

729
00:56:50,491 --> 00:56:52,576
Her siblings and I can't reach her.

730
00:56:52,660 --> 00:56:55,329
<i>Which is why I had no choice</i>
<i>but to come here.</i>

731
00:56:55,412 --> 00:56:57,832
<i>My friend's a nobody.</i>

732
00:56:57,915 --> 00:57:01,252
<i>Who knows what you could've done to her</i>
<i>because of her foolishness?</i>

733
00:57:18,769 --> 00:57:21,522
<i>I promise to be your safe space</i>

734
00:57:21,605 --> 00:57:23,607
<i>when the world feels heavy.</i>

735
00:57:24,608 --> 00:57:26,110
To be your home

736
00:57:26,819 --> 00:57:28,737
when things are uncertain.

737
00:57:28,821 --> 00:57:31,240
I give you my love eternal.

738
00:57:33,033 --> 00:57:34,285
My loyalty.

739
00:57:34,368 --> 00:57:36,704
To keep choosing you

740
00:57:37,121 --> 00:57:38,956
again and again...

741
00:57:39,582 --> 00:57:42,418
<i>in every version of tomorrow.</i>

742
00:59:36,073 --> 00:59:37,116
Taste it.

743
00:59:44,623 --> 00:59:46,542
You want to do it yourself?

744
00:59:52,923 --> 00:59:53,966
Okay.

745
00:59:56,260 --> 00:59:58,512
If you don't want me to feed you...

746
01:00:03,100 --> 01:00:04,435
Please, Beth.

747
01:00:06,687 --> 01:00:08,022
Eat.

748
01:00:09,565 --> 01:00:10,607
Okay.

749
01:00:11,358 --> 01:00:12,693
Let's eat.

750
01:00:37,801 --> 01:00:42,389
I need trust. I need loyalty.

751
01:00:42,806 --> 01:00:44,391
<i>Be careful.</i>

752
01:00:44,475 --> 01:00:45,768
<i>Be careful, Ana.</i>

753
01:00:46,477 --> 01:00:47,686
- Ana!

754
01:00:47,770 --> 01:00:49,188
Your husband is a monster.

755
01:00:49,271 --> 01:00:50,981
No!

756
01:00:51,065 --> 01:00:52,900
- <i>Stop!</i>
How sordid.

757
01:00:52,983 --> 01:00:55,736

<i>All these victims are connected to you.</i>

758
01:00:55,819 --> 01:01:00,324
Do you have evidence
that connects me to these murders?

759
01:01:00,407 --> 01:01:01,992
Ben, I know!

760
01:01:02,076 --> 01:01:03,702


761
01:01:03,786 --> 01:01:07,206
I'm not leaving Vallente
without my friend!

762
01:01:11,043 --> 01:01:12,544


763
01:01:13,796 --> 01:01:16,256
- No! Ana!

764
01:01:16,340 --> 01:01:18,759

